# --- line endings -------------------------------------------------------
# Everything above is Hugging Face LFS boilerplate. These rules are ours.
#
# Golden fixtures are compared byte-for-byte by tests. TestInitRoutesGolden
# (server/init_routes_test.go) does os.ReadFile on server/testdata/routes.golden
# and compares it against an LF-joined route list, so on a machine with
# core.autocrlf=true a fresh checkout rewrote the file to CRLF and the test
# failed with "route set drifted" before anyone had changed a line. Linux CI
# never saw it, so it only ever bit developers and agents on fresh Windows
# worktrees -- and it looked exactly like a real route-table regression.
#
# Scoped to *.golden rather than the whole testdata tree: a blanket
# "text eol=lf" there would also claim any binary fixture added later and
# corrupt it on checkout.
*.golden text eol=lf
